## Usage Pattern

```
User Request
    ↓ (auto-discovered)
Load AGENTS.md
    ↓
Evaluate triggers (session start)
    ↓
Load relevant skill(s) from ./skills/
    ↓
Load relevant things from ./things/
    ↓
Execute with consistency checks
    ↓
Validate changes
    ↓
Commit with structured message
    ↓
Evaluate triggers (post-write)
    ↓
Report changes
```

## Validation Checklist

Before committing, verify:

- [ ] Relevant skill loaded for this operation
- [ ] Domain principles maintained — semantic coherence is the agent's check (validate.thing.md → Layer 2)
- [ ] Changes scoped to appropriate things
- [ ] Commit message follows `action: description` convention

> **The Deterministic Floor:** structure (id, type, status, created), reference integrity, and schema conformance are checked by `python {framework_root}/tools/mdllm.py validate .` and enforced by the pre-commit hook (`python {framework_root}/tools/mdllm.py install-hook .` at scaffold time). Never re-perform those checks by reasoning.
